# Boardly Commerce — server-only configuration
#
# Local development does not require copying real values into this file. From
# the current Boardly Task's agent shell, run:
#   zen commerce dev --manifest boardly-commerce.json -- npm run dev
# The command fails closed outside a Task. The CLI injects all seven values
# below and a fresh, isolated BOARDLY_HOME for the child process. The Task's
# bootstrap is not copied into that home; the local private key remains only in
# daemon memory. The signer capability is ephemeral: never commit, log, print,
# or expose it to browser code.
#
# Hosted deployments provide the first four values through their server-side
# configuration. Replace the local signer helper with a KMS/HSM or
# secret-manager-backed BoardlyCommerceSigner; do not deploy a daemon lease.

BOARDLY_COMMERCE_API_URL=
BOARDLY_COMMERCE_SITE_ORIGIN=
BOARDLY_COMMERCE_SITE_ID=
BOARDLY_COMMERCE_ENVIRONMENT=
BOARDLY_COMMERCE_SIGNER_URL=
BOARDLY_COMMERCE_SIGNER_CAPABILITY=
BOARDLY_COMMERCE_SIGNER_KEY_ID=
